<Base title="Website privacy" description="How this Roost product and documentation website handles information."><main id="main" class="container legal-page"><span class="small-label">PLAIN AND SIMPLE</span><h1>Website <em>privacy.</em></h1><p>This is the Roost product and documentation website, maintained by MSR Builds. It does not offer community accounts or collect payment details. We use Google Analytics through Google Tag Manager to understand visits to this website. Optional video playback is provided by YouTube as described below.</p><h2>Documentation search</h2><p>Search runs in your browser against a static index downloaded from this website. We do not send your search terms to a search service.</p><h2>Hosting</h2><p>The hosting provider processes requests to deliver pages and protect the service. Technical information such as IP addresses may appear in its operational logs. Analytics may use cookies as described below.</p><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>Google Tag Manager loads Google Analytics on the product website and documentation pages. Google Analytics can process page views, interactions, referral information, and browser or device details, and may use cookies to measure visits. Google processes this information under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>. Analytics is installed on this product website, separately from the Roost app and shared live demo.</p><h2>Optional video playback</h2><p>The homepage intro uses a locally hosted thumbnail. YouTube’s privacy-enhanced video player loads only after you choose Play. YouTube then processes playback under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Links to GitHub, MSR Builds, and infrastructure providers take you to services with their own privacy practices. Roost communities installed by other operators are managed by those operators and are separate from this website.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Contact the project through <a href="https://github.com/msrbuilds/roost/issues">the Roost repository</a>. Please do not post credentials or private community information in a public issue.</p></main></Base>
